<title>FRANCE: Ciba, Sandoz merger to yield 600 French job cuts.</title>
<headline>Ciba, Sandoz merger to yield 600 French job cuts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The merger of Ciba Geigy AG and Sandoz AG will result in the elimination of 600 of the companies' 6,600 jobs in France, the two companies said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>The reduction in employees will take place over three years and will not include any firings. The companies will not close any of their facilities in France, they said.</p>
<p>Ciba and Sandoz said in March they intended to merge to form Novartis, the world's second-largest pharmaceutical company after Britain's Glaxo-Wellcome Plc.</p>
<p>The merger has been approved by European Union regulators but is still awaiting approval by U.S. authorities and is not likely to be final before the end of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
